          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "A Gene Expression Oscillator Acts as a Clock to Control Vertebrate Segmentation 1249  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Cell-intrinsic Timing Mechanisms Can Lead to Different Cell Fates 1251  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Cells Rarely Count Cell Divisions to Time Their Development 1252  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "MicroRNAs Can Regulate Developmental Transitions 1252  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Cell and Nuclear Size Relationships Schedule the Onset of Zygotic Gene Expression 1254  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Hormonal Signals Coordinate the Timing of Developmental Transitions 1255  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Environmental Cues Determine the Time of Flowering 1256  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Summary 1257  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "MORPHOGENESIS 1257  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Imbalance in Physical Forces Acting on Cells Drives Morphogenesis 1258  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Tension and Adhesion Determine Cell Packing Within Epithelial Sheets 1258  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Changing Patterns of Cell Adhesion Molecules Force Cells into New Arrangements 1259  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Repulsive Interactions Help Maintain Tissue Boundaries 1259  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Groups of Similar Cells Can Perform Dramatic Collective Rearrangements 1261  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Planar Cell Polarity Orients Cell Behaviors Within an Embryo 1261  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "An Epithelium Can Bend During Development to Form a Tube 1263  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Interactions Between an Epithelium and Mesenchyme Generate Branching Tubular Structures 1264  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "The Extracellular Matrix Also Influences Tissue Shape 1265  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Cell Migration Is Guided by Environmental Signals 1266  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "The Distribution of Migrant Cells Depends on Survival Factors 1267  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Cells Migrate in Groups to Achieve Large-Scale Morphogenetic Movements 1268  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Summary 1269  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "GROWTH 1269  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "The Proliferation, Death, and Size of Cells Determine Organ and Organism Size 1270  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Changes in Cell Size Usually Result from Modified Cell Cycles 1271  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Animals and Organs Can Assess and Regulate Total Cell Mass 1272  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Various Extracellular Signals Stimulate or Inhibit Growth 1273  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "The Hippo Pathway Relays Mechanical Signals Regulating Growth 1273  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Hormones Coordinate Growth Throughout the Body 1274  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "The Duration of Growth Influences Organism Size 1275  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Summary 1275  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Problems 1276  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
